<%# Filter tabs, above the table card rather than inside it.

    design.md treats a filter as chrome above the data: a plain borderless filter bar sits
    mb-4 (16px) above the table, not on its surface. These tabs were inside the card,
    which put chrome and data on one surface again - the same thing hoisting the page
    header out of the card was meant to stop.

    The rail keeps its border-b. That is the baseline the active tab's border-b-2 sits on,
    so it is structural rather than an extra divider.

    Inactive tabs carry border-b-2 border-transparent, so selecting a tab does not shift
    the row by 2px and hover:border-slate-300 has a width to apply to - it previously set
    a colour on a border with no width and rendered nothing.

    aria-current names the selected tab. It was signalled by colour alone, which leaves it
    unavailable to a screen reader and to anyone who cannot distinguish the two colours.

    Locals:
      current - the active filter: :active, :discarded or :all
      tabs    - array of [label, filter, path] %>
<div class="mb-4 flex gap-1 border-b border-slate-200" data-testid="filter-tabs">
  <% tabs.each do |label, filter, path| %>
    <% selected = current == filter %>
    <% tone = if selected
                "border-sitf-primary text-sitf-primary-dark"
              else
                "border-transparent text-slate-600 hover:border-slate-300 hover:text-slate-800"
              end %>
    <%= link_to label, path,
                aria: { current: selected ? "page" : nil },
                class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center border-b-2 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium " \
                       "focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 " \
                       "focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary #{tone}" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
